[00:21.37] Tongue tied, nerves as big as boulders
[00:23.59] Why Mom, I thought I was your soldier
[00:26.84] My brother sits by me
[00:30.60] Buckled into the carseat
[00:59.81] Feel the thirst, it's time for pulling over
[01:02.99] Into the truckstop on my daddy's shoulder
[01:06.31] Out back where they plant all the trees
[01:09.82] Ten feet away my daddy buries me
[01:13.50] GOD'S PRESENTS
[01:50.13] If my path be smooth or rugged
[01:57.35] If with thorns or roses strewn
[01:59.40] Where I go the Father seeith
[02:01.62] And He will leave me not alone
[02:03.42] If I take the wings of morning
[02:05.25] Far within the giant sea
[02:07.02] Even there His hand will leave me
[02:09.46] Even there my God will be
[02:10.91] Though the gloom of night be round me
[02:13.89] Though I cannot see my way
[02:15.35] Yet the Lord will see and guide me
[02:17.49] Because unto Him the night is day
[02:19.19] If my thought are good or evil
[02:22.55] Set me think to hide them not
[02:24.74] There is one above all seeing
[02:26.34] And He beholdth every thought
[02:28.34] And ever more my eyes beholds me
[02:31.64] And all my ways to Him are known
[02:33.78] And His loving arms enfolds me
[02:37.64] He will leave me not alone
